# PROJECT REPORT

# IoT-Based Smart Plant Health & Soil Monitoring System

## 1. Abstract

Agriculture and plant cultivation require continuous monitoring of
soil and environmental conditions. Conventional irrigation methods
often depend on manual observation and can result in overwatering or
underwatering.

This project presents an IoT-Based Smart Plant Health and Soil
Monitoring System using an ESP32 microcontroller. The system measures
soil moisture, temperature, humidity, and light intensity using
multiple sensors.

The collected data is processed by the ESP32 to determine an
environmental Plant Health Index. When soil moisture falls below a
predefined threshold, the system automatically activates a water pump
through a relay.

An OLED display provides local real-time information while Wi-Fi
connectivity provides an IoT-ready platform for remote monitoring.

---

# 2. Introduction

Modern agriculture increasingly uses IoT technologies to improve
resource efficiency and crop management.

Plants require suitable soil moisture, temperature, humidity, and
light conditions for healthy growth. Monitoring these parameters
manually is time-consuming and may result in delayed irrigation.

The proposed system automates environmental monitoring and irrigation
using an ESP32.

---

# 3. Problem Statement

Traditional plant irrigation has several limitations:

- Manual monitoring is required.
- Water may be wasted.
- Soil moisture may not be checked regularly.
- Environmental conditions are difficult to monitor continuously.
- Farmers and gardeners may not have real-time information.

The proposed system addresses these problems using sensors,
microcontroller-based processing, automatic irrigation, and IoT
connectivity.

