# 5. Proposed System

The system consists of four major sections:

## 5.1 Sensing Unit

The sensing unit consists of:

- Soil moisture sensor
- DHT22 temperature/humidity sensor
- BH1750 light sensor

These sensors collect information about the plant environment.

## 5.2 Control Unit

An ESP32 Development Board is used as the main controller.

It receives sensor data, processes it, calculates the Plant Health
Index, and controls the irrigation system.

## 5.3 Output Unit

The output section contains:

- OLED display
- RGB LED
- Relay
- Water pump

## 5.4 IoT Unit

The ESP32 connects to a Wi-Fi network and can transmit sensor data
to an IoT dashboard or cloud platform.

---

# 6. Hardware Components

## ESP32

The ESP32 is used because it provides:

- Wi-Fi
- Bluetooth
- Multiple GPIO pins
- ADC inputs
- I2C communication
- Sufficient processing capability

## Soil Moisture Sensor

The sensor measures the moisture condition of the soil.

Its analog output is connected to an ESP32 ADC pin.

## DHT22

The DHT22 measures:

- Temperature
- Relative humidity

## BH1750

The BH1750 measures ambient light intensity in lux.

## OLED Display

The OLED displays live sensor readings and the Plant Health Index.

## Relay

The relay acts as an interface between the ESP32 and the external
water pump.

## Water Pump

The pump supplies water to the plant when the soil becomes too dry.

